{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"clipboard-history","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Clipboard History","description":"Remembers what you copied and lets you paste an older item from a list.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Productivity"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onStartup"],"permissions":["clipboard"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"clipboardHistory.show","title":"Paste from History...","category":"Clipboard History"},{"command":"clipboardHistory.pasteLast","title":"Paste the Previous Clipboard Item","category":"Clipboard History"},{"command":"clipboardHistory.copy","title":"Copy an Earlier Item Again...","category":"Clipboard History"},{"command":"clipboardHistory.togglePause","title":"Pause or Resume Recording","category":"Clipboard History"},{"command":"clipboardHistory.clear","title":"Clear History","category":"Clipboard History"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"clipboardHistory.show","key":"Ctrl+Alt+V"}],"configuration":{"title":"Clipboard History","properties":{"clipboardHistory.max":{"type":"number","default":50,"description":"How many items to remember (5 to 200)."},"clipboardHistory.persist":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Keep the last 50 items between sessions. Off by default so copied passwords do not stay on disk."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Clipboard History: remembers what you copied and lets you paste an older item. It checks the clipboard every second or two\n// while Ferrum is open, so it needs the clipboard permission. Nothing leaves your computer.\n\n/** Adds an item to the front, removing an older copy of the same text, and keeps `max` items. */\nfunction push(list, text, max) {\n  const t = String(text);\n  if (!t.trim()) return list;\n  const next = [{ text: t, at: Date.now() }, ...list.filter((x) => x.text !== t)];\n  return next.slice(0, Math.max(1, max));\n}\n\n/** A one-line preview for the list. */\nfunction preview(text, n = 90) {\n  const one = text.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n  return one.length > n ? one.slice(0, n - 1) + '…' : one;\n}\n\nfunction ago(at, now = Date.now()) {\n  const s = Math.max(0, Math.round((now - at) / 1000));\n  if (s < 60) return 'just now';\n  if (s < 3600) return Math.floor(s / 60) + ' min ago';\n  if (s < 86400) return Math.floor(s / 3600) + ' h ago';\n  return Math.floor(s / 86400) + ' d ago';\n}\n\n/** Text that looks like a secret is not stored: long random strings, private keys, tokens. */\nfunction looksSecret(text) {\n  const t = text.trim();\n  if (/-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----/.test(t)) return true;\n  if (/^(sk|pk|ghp|gho|ghs|glpat|xox[abp]|AKIA)[-_A-Za-z0-9]{16,}$/.test(t)) return true;\n  if (/^eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]*$/.test(t)) return true;\n  return false;\n}\n\nexports._test = { push, preview, ago, looksSecret };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  let history = [];\n  let paused = false;\n  let last = null;\n  let timer = null;\n  const max = () => Math.min(200, Math.max(5, Number(ferrum.settings.get('clipboardHistory.max')) || 50));\n  const persist = () => ferrum.settings.get('clipboardHistory.persist') === true;\n  const reg = (id, fn) => context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register(id, fn));\n\n  function status() {\n    ferrum.window.setStatusBar('clipboardHistory.status', { text: paused ? 'Clipboard: paused' : 'Clipboard: ' + history.length, tooltip: 'Clipboard History: click to browse', command: 'clipboardHistory.show' });\n  }\n\n  async function poll() {\n    if (paused) return;\n    let text;\n    try { text = await ferrum.clipboard.readText(); } catch { return; }\n    if (typeof text !== 'string' || text === last) return;\n    last = text;\n    if (!text.trim() || text.length > 100000 || looksSecret(text)) return;\n    history = push(history, text, max());\n    status();\n    if (persist()) await ferrum.storage.set('history', history.slice(0, 50));\n  }\n\n  (async () => {\n    if (persist()) history = (await ferrum.storage.get('history', [])).filter((x) => x && typeof x.text === 'string');\n    try { last = await ferrum.clipboard.readText(); } catch { last = null; }\n    status();\n    timer = setInterval(poll, 1500);\n    context.subscriptions.push({ dispose: () => clearInterval(timer) });\n  })();\n\n  reg('clipboardHistory.show', async () => {\n    if (!history.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Nothing has been copied since Ferrum started.');\n    const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(\n      history.map((h, i) => ({ label: preview(h.text), detail: h.text.length + ' characters', description: ago(h.at), i })),\n      { placeholder: 'Pick what to paste at the cursor' },\n    );\n    if (!pick) return;\n    const item = history[pick.i];\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (doc) await ferrum.editor.insert(item.text);\n    else ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a file to paste into.', 'warn');\n  });\n  reg('clipboardHistory.copy', async () => {\n    if (!history.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Nothing has been copied since Ferrum started.');\n    const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(history.map((h, i) => ({ label: preview(h.text), description: ago(h.at), i })), { placeholder: 'Pick what to copy again' });\n    if (!pick) return;\n    last = history[pick.i].text;\n    await ferrum.clipboard.writeText(last);\n    ferrum.window.showMessage('Copied again. Press Ctrl+V anywhere.');\n  });\n  reg('clipboardHistory.pasteLast', async () => {\n    if (history.length < 2) return ferrum.window.showMessage('There is no earlier item yet.');\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (doc) await ferrum.editor.insert(history[1].text);\n  });\n  reg('clipboardHistory.clear', async () => {\n    history = [];\n    await ferrum.storage.set('history', []);\n    status();\n    ferrum.window.showMessage('Clipboard history cleared.');\n  });\n  reg('clipboardHistory.togglePause', () => {\n    paused = !paused;\n    status();\n    ferrum.window.showMessage(paused ? 'Clipboard History is paused. New copies are not recorded.' : 'Clipboard History is recording again.');\n  });\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Clipboard History\n\nFerrum checks the clipboard every second or two while it is open and keeps what you copied, newest first. **Paste from History...** shows the list; pick an item to insert it at the cursor. **Copy an Earlier Item Again...** puts an old item back on the clipboard to paste anywhere. The status bar shows how many items are kept; click it to browse.\n\n## Privacy\n\n- It needs the **clipboard** permission, because that is how it can read what you copied. Everything stays on your computer.\n- The history is **in memory only**, and is gone when you close Ferrum, unless you turn on `clipboardHistory.persist`.\n- Things that look like secrets are **never recorded**: private keys, JWT tokens and common API key formats. Other text is recorded as is, so use **Pause or Resume Recording** before copying a password, and **Clear History** when you are done.\n- Items over 100,000 characters are skipped.\n\nIt only sees the clipboard while Ferrum is running, and it cannot know what you copied in a program that was closed.\n"}}}